menu "MAO battery"

    config MAO_BATTERY_CRITICAL_MV
        int "Critical cell voltage (mV, loaded)"
        range 3000 3800
        default 3550
        help
            On battery, a cell voltage below this (three gauge readings in a
            row, or SOC <= 2 %) posts MAO_EVENT_BATTERY_CRITICAL and the
            application puts MAO into its critical-battery deep sleep.
            Provisional floor 3.55 V under load from M5 Gate C (the panel and
            radio peaks must not reach the regulator's dropout / the 3V3
            UVLO). VERIFY AT BRING-UP against the measured discharge curve.

    config MAO_BATTERY_CRITICAL_SLEEP
        bool "Deep sleep on a critical battery"
        default y
        help
            After MAO_EVENT_BATTERY_CRITICAL the application lets MAO fall
            asleep (the resting mark, then deep sleep) with only the press
            and a recheck timer as wake sources.

    config MAO_BATTERY_CRITICAL_RECHECK_MIN
        int "Critical-battery deep sleep: recheck timer (minutes)"
        depends on MAO_BATTERY_CRITICAL_SLEEP
        range 5 1440
        default 60
        help
            USB cannot wake the A1 from deep sleep (VBUS_SENSE is not an RTC
            pad), so a timer wakes it to see whether it is being charged.

endmenu
